  "post": {
    "caption": "This golden hat may count months. The Berlin Gold Hat is about 3,000 years old, from the Late Bronze Age, and stands about 74 centimeters tall. It weighs only about half a kilo. It was hammered from one sheet of gold, thin as paper, with flat bronze bands to strengthen it. Rings and discs are punched into the gold in patterns, and researchers read them as a calendar of sun and moon. One reading says it tracks a cycle of 19 years. It is kept in the Neues Museum in Berlin, and only four gold cone hats like it are known.",
